# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Flaviano Della Pia et al. (2025). Accurate and efficient machine learning interatomic potentials for finite temperature modelling of molecular crystals.
#   Chemical Science. doi:10.1039/d5sc01325a  arXiv:2502.15530v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2502.15530v2 (sha256 e90a8127e4567ce6...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 312 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/pia2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: MACE-MP-0 (medium) fine-tuned with about 150-360
# vdW-DF2 structures per system for the 23 X23 molecular crystals, for
# paracetamol, aspirin and squaric acid, for the ice polymorphs (revPBE-D3)
# and as one general X23 model, with training and validation energy,
# force and stress RMSEs (Tables S27, S33, S34, S36). Sublimation
# enthalpies, lattice energies and equations of state are properties, not
# error metrics.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

