###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training data for each crystal cost about 30 CPU node-hours (Ice Lake,
# 76 cores) on average; per-system DFT and fine-tuning costs (GPU-hours on
# an NVIDIA A100-SXM-80GB) are tabulated in Table S26.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Stress RMSEs are in meV/A3, for which the schema has no unit; they are recorded with unit null. Energy RMSEs below 0.01 meV/atom are printed as 0.00 by the training script (Table S27 note).
# - The ice training set contains 32 structures per DMC-ICE13 phase plus 48 water clusters (total not stated). Per-system fine-tuning costs of Table S26 are not encoded as numbers because the table body is not legible in the text layer.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/pia2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

